  "facts": [
    {
      "id": "codex-through-runtime",
      "claim": "Codex Chat, Responses and both streams are served through an llmgw-core runtime.Runtime held by providers.Runtime: core's Codex vertical sends upstream, the iam credential store resolves and loads connections, a tokenstore.Coordinator refreshes under the SQLite lease, and core's NewCodexRefresh refreshes with each connection's stored client. The gateway's Codex session source, 401 refresh transport and Codex refresh-lock table are removed. Upstream request bytes are unchanged; the characterization goldens pass unchanged.",
      "status": "observed",
      "evidence": {
        "source": "go/internal/providers/core_runtime.go, codex.go, codex_credentials.go, codex_call.go; go/internal/api/testdata unchanged"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "parity-rules",
      "claim": "A connection without a stored client is refused refresh with the existing reauthorization error; each credential fetch is pinned to the account of its first load, so a concurrent re-login fails the request instead of switching accounts; console refresh loads the record and calls Coordinator.Rejected; terminal refresh errors revoke through RevokeIfCurrent and the owner's caches are forgotten after a revoke or stored refresh; a failed refresh after a 401 is reported as before.",
      "status": "observed",
      "evidence": {
        "source": "go/internal/providers/codex_credentials.go; codex_test.go and codex_runtime_test.go"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "probe-observation",
      "claim": "Probe and verify checks get the connection and revision a Codex call used from a request-scoped collector fed by the credential store and the Runtime's evidence sink, including the revision after a mid-request refresh; outside a collector the sink records nothing, so inference records no evidence, as before.",
      "status": "observed",
      "evidence": {
        "source": "go/internal/providers/credential_evidence.go and its test"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "error-path-deviations",
      "claim": "Three error paths differ: an expired Codex token without a refresh token fails before sending instead of being sent; a catalog 401 on such a token reports catalog_authentication_failed and other failed catalog refreshes catalog_refresh_failed; and a Codex call that fails before loading any credential returns no observation instead of a zero-revision one. None affects a successful request, the CLI, health or the public models list.",
      "status": "observed",
      "evidence": {
        "source": "go/internal/providers/codex.go and codex_test.go"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "suite",
      "claim": "The full Go suite passes with HTTP_PROXY and HTTPS_PROXY unreachable with unchanged characterization goldens; the providers iam.* budget moves from 82 to 75; gofmt, vet, govulncheck (0 reachable), check-docs and git diff --check pass.",
      "status": "observed",
      "evidence": {
        "source": "local gate run on the reviewed head"
      }
    }
  ],
